<code>assert fromIndex >= -1 => \forall int i; this.previousClearBit(fromIndex)+1 <= i && i <= fromIndex; this.get(i);</code>

However, the above assertion seems incorrect because it states that all bits between the result and `fromIndex` should be set to `true`, which contradicts the purpose of `previousClearBit`. Instead, the correct assertion should state that all bits between the result and `fromIndex` should be set to `false`.

Here is the corrected assert statement:

<code>assert fromIndex >= -1 => \forall int i; this.previousClearBit(fromIndex)+1 <= i && i <= fromIndex; !this.get(i);</code>--------------------<code>assert fromIndex >= -1 ==> \forall int i; this.result < i && i <= fromIndex; this.get(i) == true;</code>

However, since `this.result` is not directly accessible, we need to use `\result` to refer to the return value of the method. Therefore, the correct assert statement would be:

<code>assert fromIndex >= -1 ==> \forall int i; \result < i && i <= fromIndex; this.get(i) == true;</code>--------------------<code>assert fromIndex >= -1 => \forall int i; \result < i && i <= fromIndex; this.get(i);</code>--------------------